[["text","LESSON 08 / 31 • ORIGINAL CHECKLIST"],["heading","8. Heaps and priority queues"],["text","English: A heap maintains a priority ordering; a priority queue removes the highest-priority item"],["text","first."],["sinhala","","සිංහල: Priority අනුවෙ item එකක් මුලින් 9බාගන්න structure එකක්.",342],["text","Real-world example: Emergency ticket priority"],["code","      10"],["code","     /  \\"],["code","   30    20"],["heading","Java example / illustration"],["code","PriorityQueue<Integer> q = new PriorityQueue<>();\nq.offer(30); q.offer(10); q.offer(20);\nSystem.out.println(q.poll()); // 10"],["heading","Complexity and trade-offs"],["text","Peek O(1); insert/remove root O(log n)."],["heading","Interview question"],["heading","Is a heap fully sorted?"],["text","No. It guarantees a parent-child priority property."],["heading","Quick practice"],["text","Explain this concept aloud, trace the example, and describe when you would choose this"],["text","structure over an alternative."]]